    "created_at": "2016-02-19T17:52:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-19T17:52:26Z",
    "body": "I was looking at the proposed definition of \"optionally truncate a simple dialog string\" and it says:\n\n> <p>To <dfn>optionally truncate a simple dialog string</dfn> <var>s</var>, return either <var>s</var> itself or any leading substring of <var>s</var>.\n\nThat's not actually how Chromium truncates dialog strings today. Our truncation function, `gfx::ElideString`, actually chops out the middle of the string and replaces it with a \"...\". If you're going to tweak the spec to allow Chromium to officially do what it does today, can you allow it to _actually_ do what it does today? :)\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
